    "description": "Vintage Portuguese hinged bracelet by Topázio, featuring intricate filigree and cannetille-style wirework with applied bead and floral decoration. The bracelet has a warm gilt/gold-wash finish over silver, with areas of wear revealing the silver beneath.\nInterior is marked “TOPAZIO / STERLING / PORTUGAL” and the clasp tongue bears additional Portuguese assay and maker’s punches. Topázio was produced by Ferreira Marques & Irmão of Porto, Portugal, a noted Portuguese silver manufacturer.Metal content and gold-tone finish have not been independently tested; buyer should rely on photos and markings.\nFeatures a hinged design with box-style closure and safety chain. Weighs approximately 38.8 grams / 1.368 oz.\nLikely mid-20th century, approximately 1940s–1960s.\nGood vintage condition with expected surface wear, oxidation/patina, scratches, and wear to the gilt finish consistent with age and use. Clasp, hinge, and safety chain appear intact. Fine decorative wirework appears substantially complete. Please review all photos carefully for condition and markings.",
